TI  - Bronchial epithelial-myoepithelial carcinoma.
PG  - 689-91
AB  - An epithelial-myoepithelial tumor is an extremely rare pulmonary neoplasm. Only 
      21 cases have been reported to date. This report presents a case of left main 
      bronchial epithelial-myoepithelial carcinoma in a 43-year-old woman. No 
      mediastinal lymph nodes were enlarged in computed tomographic scan, and no tumor 
      growth was noted beyond the bronchial cartilage layer by endobronchial ultrasound 
      imaging. This report highlights the usefulness of endobronchial ultrasound 
      imaging for determining the depth of tumor invasion and choosing an alternative 
      approach to surgical resection.
