AB  - Endobronchial thymoma is an exceedingly rare presentation. We report a 
      70-year-old woman undergoing bronchoscopy for dyspnea and a computed tomographic 
      scan believed to be most consistent with a right lower lobe neoplasm. 
      Thoracoscopy was ultimately required for diagnosis.
