DP  - 2007 Feb
TI  - Transverse bronchoplasty of the membranous wall after resection of an 
      endobronchial hamartoma.
PG  - 703-4
AB  - Lung hamartomas are rare benign tumors of the bronchi. Their management consists 
      of bronchoscopic excision or removal through a thoracotomy and bronchotomy 
      whenever there is a large tumor totally obstructing the bronchial lumen. As a 
      lung-sparing procedure is usually the aim, various bronchoplastic techniques have 
      been described, providing a functional lumen of the repaired bronchus. We 
      describe a simple technique that can be safely undertaken to preserve a 
      satisfactory diameter of the bronchus or trachea and prevent a stenosis at the 
      site of repair.
