DP  - 2008 Mar
TI  - Adenocarcinoma with epidermal growth factor receptor gene mutations in three 
      siblings.
PG  - 311-3
LID - 10.1097/JTO.0b013e3181653cce [doi]
AB  - Sensitivity to an inhibitor of epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) kinase 
      strongly correlates with EGFR somatic mutations in non-small cell lung cancer. 
      These mutations are frequently found in patients with adenocarcinoma, never- or 
      light-smokers, women, and East Asians. In this study, we show an aggregation of 
      three non-small cell lung cancer cases with EGFR gene mutations in one family. 
      The subjects were all female, never- or light-smokers with adenocarcinoma. Two of 
      the patients responded to treatment with gefitinib. A genetic study of these 
      cases would be useful in elucidating genetic susceptibility to lung cancer in 
      persons with EGFR mutations.
