DP  - 2010 Feb
TI  - Removal of long-term tracheal stents with excellent tracheal healing.
PG  - 598-9
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2009.07.040 [doi]
AB  - Covered metallic endobronchial stents are increasingly used in the management of 
      diverse large airway pathology and once deployed they are considered permanent. 
      Long-term complications of stent fracture and airway granulation tissue formation 
      may necessitate stent removal. We describe successful endoscopic removal of the 
      Ultraflex expandable tracheal metallic stents (Microvasive; Boston Scientific, 
      Natick, MA) in 5 patients at 105, 84, 50, 38, and 21 months after deployment, 
      with excellent tracheal healing and clearance of granulation tissue noted at 6 
      weeks after removal in each patient.
