TI  - Pneumocystis pneumonia in a patient with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) 
      treated with pemetrexed containing regimen.
PG  - 240-2
AB  - Pneumocystis pneumonia is typically life-threatening in immunocompromised 
      patients. It is relatively uncommon in patients with lung cancer. We report a 
      case of pneumocystis pneumonia in a patient with advanced stage non-small cell 
      lung cancer (NSCLC) following treatment with concurrent chemoradiation with a 
      pemetrexed containing regimen. To our knowledge, this is the first report on 
      pneumocystis pneumonia following administration of pemetrexed containing regimen.
