IS  - 0169-5002 (Linking)
VI  - 58
IP  - 2
DP  - 2007 Nov
TI  - Use of bronchoscopic electrocautery in removing an endotracheal metastasis.
PG  - 286-90
AB  - Bronchoscopic electrocautery is an easy, safe and rapid local method for the 
      removal of a tracheal metastasis. Recently, we experienced a case of papillary 
      serous carcinoma of the ovary with tracheal metastasis in a 45-year-old woman. 
      Twelve years after the initial diagnosis of ovarian cancer, the patient presented 
      with dyspnea. A chest CT scan showed that the trachea was nearly obstructed with 
      a polypoid mass. The mass, later shown to be a metastatic papillary serous 
      carcinoma, was removed by flexible bronchoscopic electrocautery with a snare. To 
      our knowledge, this report is the first to describe the successful removal of an 
      endotracheal metastasis of ovarian cancer using bronchoscopic electrocautery.
