TI  - Prevalence of brain metastases immediately before prophylactic cranial 
      irradiation in limited disease small cell lung cancer patients with complete 
      remission to chemoradiotherapy: a single institution experience.
PG  - 652-5
LID - 10.1097/JTO.0b013e3181757a76 [doi]
AB  - This single-center study investigated the prevalence of brain metastases 
      immediately before prophylactic cranial irradiation in 40 consecutive limited 
      disease small cell lung cancer complete responders to chemoradiotherapy and 
      revealed that 13/40 (32.5%; 95% confidence interval: 18-47%) patients suffer 
      relapse with brain metastases and show a significantly worse prognosis than those 
      without detected brain metastases.
