TI  - Radical Carinal Resection for a Glomic Tumor.
PG  - e143-5
LID - S0003-4975(16)00026-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2016.01.023 [doi]
AB  - We report the case of a 33-year-old woman who presented with increasing dyspnea 
      secondary to a tumor arising from the carina. After desobstruction by 
      bronchoscopy, the pathologic analysis revealed a glomic tumor. Carinal resection 
      and reconstruction were performed with venoarterial extracorporeal membrane 
      oxygenation support. The patient's postoperative course was uneventful, and the 
      long-term result was excellent.
