TI  - Total tracheal resection for long-segment benign tracheal stenosis.
PG  - 654-6
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2007.08.052 [doi]
AB  - Tracheal resection for long benign tracheal stenosis is challenging because of 
      the lack of a suitable replacement to facilitate tension-free anastomosis. We 
      describe a patient with a 6-cm post-tuberculous tracheal stricture, severely 
      debilitated post-recurrent bronchoscopic intervention. Staged resection 
      facilitated near-total tracheal resection with primary anastomosis and complete 
      symptom resolution.
