TI  - An unusual cause of breathlessness after lobectomy for lung cancer.
PG  - e13-4
AB  - Localized bronchomalacia as a cause of breathlessness after lobectomy is an 
      unusual complication. This condition was diagnosed with bronchoscopy and 
      delineated by spiral computed tomographic scan. Stenting the lesion resulted in a 
      successful outcome.
