LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2018.05.024 [doi]
AB  - A 21-year-old patient presented with a short history of fatigue and dyspnea on a 
      background of double-lung transplantation for cystic fibrosis and preexisting 
      chronic superior vena cava obstruction. Computed tomography of the chest 
      demonstrated a 3-cm mass occluding the right pulmonary veins, with associated 
      right upper and lower lobe pulmonary parenchymal infiltrates. Two invasive 
      procedures were performed, with similar complications in both procedures.
