TI  - Massive Hemoptysis From an Aortobronchial Fistula Secondary to BCG-Related 
      Mycotic Thoracic Aortic Aneurysm.
PG  - 350-2
LID - S0003-4975(15)00489-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2015.03.053 [doi]
AB  - Intravesical bacillus Calmette-Guérin (BCG) is first-line therapy for noninvasive 
      bladder cancer. Although side effects are rare, systemic dissemination can result 
      in mycotic aneurysms. We report the case of a rapidly developing thoracic aortic 
      mycotic aneurysm presenting as massive hemoptysis from an aortobronchial fistula. 
      This case was unusual in its location, rapidity of development, and failure of 
      medical therapy. The diagnostic challenges and the need for a high index of 
      suspicion are discussed.
