TI  - Controlled Trachea Suspension for Tracheomalacia After Resection of Large 
      Anterior Mediastinal Mass.
PG  - 2225-7
LID - S0003-4975(15)00223-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2015.01.067 [doi]
AB  - Tracheomalacia is a disorder of the large airways that is often caused by a large 
      anterior mediastinal mass. This study describes 7 patients who underwent 
      controlled trachea suspension as a surgical intervention to prevent severe 
      tracheomalacia and provide potent relief of airway symptoms. All patients 
      recovered well. The results demonstrate this procedure may be safe and effective 
      for resection of a large mediastinal mass compressing the trachea with collapsed 
      segments.
