OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20061114
LR  - 20221207
IS  - 1552-6259 (Electronic)
IS  - 0003-4975 (Linking)
VI  - 82
IP  - 5
DP  - 2006 Nov
TI  - Management dilemmas due to a paratracheal follicular dendritic cell tumor.
PG  - 1898-900
AB  - Follicular dendritic cell tumors are rare cancers of the lymph nodes of the head 
      and neck. Despite a relatively high rate of recurrence, these neoplasms have a 
      limited impact on the airways because they can be potentially cured by surgical 
      resection. We present the case of a young woman with an unresectable follicular 
      dendritic cell tumor involving the paratracheal region causing upper airway 
      obstruction and respiratory failure. This malignant tumor created numerous 
      management dilemmas and therapeutic challenges related to the unstable airway and 
      the need for tracheal stenting to bypass the airway obstruction.
