TI  - Treatment of severe carinal stenosis with overlapping metallic endoprosthesis.
PG  - 1335-6
AB  - A 50-year-old man presented with respiratory distress from central airway 
      compression secondary to malignant mediastinal adenopathy. The stenosis involved 
      the carinal triangle and created residual luminal diameters of 6 mm, 6 mm, and 
      pinhole in the distal trachea and right and left mainstem bronchi, respectively. 
      Airway patency at the carina was restored successfully with a stenting method 
      that uses two overlapping Wall stents.
