TI  - Tracheal malignant melanoma: successful outcome with tracheal resection.
PG  - 308-10
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2008.01.056 [doi]
AB  - Primary tracheal malignant melanomas are uncommon neoplasms: only five cases have 
      been reported. Different therapeutic approaches are described, with a short life 
      expectancy observed. We report a case of a young woman with a primary tracheal 
      malignant melanoma who underwent complete tracheal resection and is free of 
      disease 4 years after surgical treatment.
