TI  - Tracheal stenosis caused by retrosternal dislocation of the right clavicle.
PG  - 685-7
AB  - A 17-year-old woman was admitted to our institution because of tracheal stenosis. 
      She had undergone tracheostomy after a traffic accident, but the stenosis had 
      persisted. Chest computed tomography showed retrosternal dislocation of the right 
      sternoclavicular joint and compression of the trachea by the medial head of the 
      right clavicle. To relieve the tracheal compression, 3 cm of the medial head of 
      the clavicle was resected. The dyspnea disappeared completely, allowing closure 
      of the tracheostomy. Posterior dislocation of the sternoclavicular joint and 
      tracheal stenosis due to compression by the dislocated clavicle is rare.
