PMID- 18355548
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20080416
LR  - 20220310
IS  - 1552-6259 (Electronic)
IS  - 0003-4975 (Linking)
VI  - 85
IP  - 4
DP  - 2008 Apr
TI  - Idiopathic tracheal stenosis: successful outcome with antigastroesophageal reflux 
      disease therapy.
PG  - 1438-9
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2007.10.032 [doi]
AB  - There is controversial evidence that gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) is an 
      etiologic factor for idiopathic laryngotracheal stenosis. We present the case of 
      a 44-year-old woman with symptomatic tracheal stenosis managed as idiopathic 
      stenosis. She underwent six endoscopic dilations during 1 year, and before 
      surgery she underwent 24-hour esophageal pH monitoring that documented GERD. 
      Anti-GERD treatment was started, which was confirmed as effective with 24-hour 
      esophageal pH monitoring 3 months later. At 2-year follow-up the patient remained 
      free of symptoms and no additional airway procedure was necessary. A close 
      relationship between anti-GERD therapy and clinical outcome was noted.
