VI  - 104
IP  - 5
DP  - 2017 Nov
TI  - Complications of Endobronchial Ultrasound-Guided Transbronchial Needle 
      Aspiration.
PG  - e363-e365
LID - S0003-4975(17)30849-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2017.06.015 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial ultrasound-guided transbronchial needle aspiration (EBUS-TBNA) is 
      considered useful for the staging and diagnosis of lung cancer or thoracic lymph 
      node enlargement; however, little is known about its complications. Between July 
      2009 and November 2016, 413 patients underwent EBUS-TBNA, and four complications 
      (0.97%) occurred. Here we report four cases involving complications of EBUS-TBNA, 
      including mediastinitis (n = 2), obstructive pneumonia (n = 1), and airway 
      obstruction requiring admission to the intensive care unit (n = 1). All patients 
      recovered with appropriate medical treatment. Despite their low incidence, the 
      complications associated with EBUS-TBNA can be serious.
