LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2021.08.011 [doi]
AB  - Pneumothorax and persistent air leak are documented complications of severe acute 
      respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 infection. Patients who fall into this 
      category are often poor candidates for invasive thoracic surgical intervention. 
      Endobronchial valves offer an effective and less invasive treatment option and 
      can successfully treat persistent air leak and support the weaning of patients 
      with severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 pneumonia off ventilation.
