PMID- 16863797
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20060816
LR  - 20060725
IS  - 1552-6259 (Electronic)
IS  - 0003-4975 (Linking)
VI  - 82
IP  - 2
DP  - 2006 Aug
TI  - Pulmonary resection after successful downstaging with photodynamic therapy.
PG  - 722-4
AB  - Photodynamic therapy (PDT) is a treatment option for lung cancer that involves 
      the administration of a photosensitizing agent and selective, bronchoscopic 
      delivery of light to tumor tissue that has retained the agent. Currently, PDT is 
      used either to treat microinvasive endobronchial nonsmall cell lung cancer 
      (NSCLC) or to palliate patients with completely or partially obstructing 
      endobronchial NSCLC. Herein is a case of PDT that successfully downstaged an 
      obstructing endobronchial NSCLC, thereby enabling a complete resection. At 9 
      months postoperatively, the patient was treated for a chest wall recurrence with 
      no evidence of disease in the airway or mediastinum.
