TI  - Polypoid endobronchial Hodgkin lymphoma with an initial response to photodynamic 
      therapy.
PG  - 940-2
AB  - Endobronchial presentation of Hodgkin lymphoma is rare and can be confused 
      clinically and radiographically with pulmonary small cell carcinoma. We present a 
      case of an obstructive endobronchial presentation of nodular sclerosing classic 
      Hodgkin lymphoma, initially misdiagnosed as small cell carcinoma, with 
      endobronchial vasculitis and associated hemoptysis. Photodynamic therapy relieved 
      the obstruction before induction of tumor-specific therapy. This case 
      demonstrates the successful use of photodynamic therapy in obstructive 
      endobronchial Hodgkin lymphoma.
