TI  - Transthoracic esophagectomy using endobronchial blocker after previous 
      pneumonectomy.
PG  - 723-5
LID - S0003-4975(13)01665-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2013.07.054 [doi]
AB  - Esophagectomy after pneumonectomy is very rare. We present a case of 
      esophagectomy for esophageal cancer after left pneumonectomy. By application of 
      an endobronchial blocker, satisfactory results were achieved and the 
      disadvantages of extracorporeal membrane oxygenation, cardiopulmonary bypass, and 
      other ventilation methods were avoided.
