PG  - 1816-9
LID - S0003-4975(14)01518-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2014.06.111 [doi]
AB  - A patient diagnosed with pulmonary embolism had persistent symptoms despite 
      adequate therapy. Tissue sampling with endobronchial ultrasound-guided needle 
      aspiration revealed endovascular metastasis from a prior early-stage colorectal 
      cancer. We describe the challenges in the diagnosis and workup of suspected tumor 
      emboli.
