TI  - Primary Neuroendocrine Carcinoma of the Middle Mediastinum Involving the Right 
      Main Pulmonary Artery.
PG  - 1594-6
LID - S0003-4975(15)01075-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2015.05.130 [doi]
AB  - Primary neuroendocrine neoplasms of the mediastinum are extremely rare. We report 
      the case of a 54-year-old woman who presented with dyspnea and was found to have 
      a 6.8-cm tumor completely obliterating the right main pulmonary artery. Analysis 
      of an endobronchial ultrasound fine-needle aspiration revealed a neuroendocrine 
      tumor. A positron emission tomography scan showed no evidence of distant disease. 
      The patient underwent surgical resection with reconstruction of the right main 
      pulmonary artery with a Dacron (DuPont, Wilmington, DE) graft, followed by 
      chemoradiotherapy. We discuss the presentation and management of this patient and 
      review the current treatment options of primary neuroendocrine carcinomas of the 
      mediastinum.
