TI  - Thoracoscopic tracheal resection and reconstruction for adenoid cystic carcinoma.
PG  - e15-7
LID - S0003-4975(14)01624-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2014.06.118 [doi]
AB  - We describe a novel technique of thoracoscopic circumferential tracheal resection 
      and end-to-end anastomosis. A 60-year-old woman presented with wheezing and 
      progressive dyspnea. Computed tomography scan revealed a mass at the lower 
      trachea, and a nitinol mesh stent was implanted by bronchoscopy. After 2 weeks, a 
      complete thoracoscopic tracheal resection and reconstruction was performed. The 
      postoperative course was uneventful. The final pathologic examination confirmed 
      the diagnosis of primary adenoid cystic carcinoma of the trachea.
