TI  - A completion sleeve bilobectomy for nonstump postlobectomy bronchopleural 
      fistula.
PG  - 2112-4
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2007.11.062 [doi]
AB  - We present a novel approach for treatment of nonstump postlobectomy bronchial 
      fistula. Our patient had right lower lobectomy for T3 N2 M0 adenocarcinoma. An 
      increased air leak developed 8 days later, and bronchoscopy revealed the presence 
      of a bronchial fistula. On reexploration, the bronchial stump was intact, and the 
      membranous part of the bronchus intermedius was sloughed up to the opening of the 
      upper lobe bronchus. A middle lobectomy with sleeve resection of the bronchus 
      intermedius and part of the right main bronchus was performed, and the upper lobe 
      was reanastomosed to the right main bronchus. The patient's postoperative course 
      was uneventful, and follow-up bronchoscopy showed an intact healed anastomosis.
