TI  - Vaping Contributing to Postoperative Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome.
PG  - e169-e171
LID - S0003-4975(21)00114-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2021.01.021 [doi]
AB  - We report the case of an 18-year-old male patient with a history of bicuspid 
      aortic valve with severe aortic insufficiency who had undergone a Ross procedure 
      1 year prior but subsequently developed stenosis of the pulmonary homograft 
      necessitating conduit replacement. His postoperative course was complicated by 
      acute respiratory distress syndrome. Bronchoscopy revealed significant mucus 
      plugging without identification of contributing pathogen. Further evaluation 
      revealed a history of electronic cigarette use not identified preoperatively and 
      thought to be largely contributory to his postoperative complications. This case 
      highlights the importance of screening preoperatively for electronic cigarette 
      use and counseling on cessation before surgical procedures.
