TI  - Extratracheal biodegradable splint to treat life-threatening tracheomalacia.
PG  - 1446-8
AB  - A 9-month-old girl presented with life-threatening acute respiratory failure 1 
      week after the surgical correction of a double aortic arch, which was due to a 
      severe bulging of the pars membranacea into the lumen of the trachea that 
      produced a complete obstruction of the lower trachea. Under cardiopulmonary 
      bypass, a Y-shaped posterior biodegradable splint was placed behind the trachea 
      and sutured to the posterior trachea, and a simultaneous right aortic arch 
      aortopexy was performed. Thereafter, the child recovered normal respiratory 
      function. Follow-up bronchoscopy showed a posterior dip at the splint level and 
      an asymptomatic persistent posterior compression of the right main bronchus.
