TI  - Very unusual case of post-traumatic chylothorax.
PG  - 1488-91
AB  - Chylothorax is a rare disease caused by both traumatic and nontraumatic events. 
      Chylothorax can cause cardiopulmonary abnormalities and significant nutritional, 
      metabolic, and immunologic consequences. We present an exceptional case of 
      chylothorax due to penetrating chest trauma. The diagnosis was made by 
      thoracentesis. Conservative management with nothing by mouth and total parenteral 
      nutrition failed; therefore the patient needed surgical closure of the duct leak.
